\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The model kinds the pipeline represents and executes, one row per kind. Notation blocks are the parameterization each kind declares; exemplar folders are the committed corpus under \breaktt {input/gnn\_files/}. Renderer(s)/Executor(s) cells are generated from the registry flags (see tbl.~\ref {tbl:framework_capability}): the two parameterization rows carry their own flag sets, excluding continuous-only targets from categorical coverage. These flags do not establish universal multi-agent support: THRML accepts independent categorical components, and coupled models require a backend-specific representation and acceptance evidence. Native independent linear-Gaussian agent exemplars are verified on JAX and RxInfer in the v4 acceptance ledger; \texttt {recursive/} is reserved for bounded \texttt {-\/-autonomous} proposal-loop runs and holds no committed models.}}{5}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tbl:model_kinds}{{1}{5}{The model kinds the pipeline represents and executes, one row per kind. Notation blocks are the parameterization each kind declares; exemplar folders are the committed corpus under \protect \breaktt {input/gnn\_files/}. Renderer(s)/Executor(s) cells are generated from the registry flags (see tbl.~\ref {tbl:framework_capability}): the two parameterization rows carry their own flag sets, excluding continuous-only targets from categorical coverage. These flags do not establish universal multi-agent support: THRML accepts independent categorical components, and coupled models require a backend-specific representation and acceptance evidence. Native independent linear-Gaussian agent exemplars are verified on JAX and RxInfer in the v4 acceptance ledger; \protect \texttt {recursive/} is reserved for bounded \protect \texttt {-\/-autonomous} proposal-loop runs and holds no committed models}{table.1}{}}
