\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The Triple Play: one GNN text specification (left) and its three coordinated projections (right) --- the human-readable text form, graphical model visualizations, and executable simulation code. All three arrows originate at the same source box to show their shared parsed input. Source binding, parameter validation, and semantic-fidelity checks provide evidence of agreement among the projections. The executable node summarizes 12 of 12 registered render targets with implemented Step 12 execution adapters and previews three by name; execution depends on runtime readiness, admitted model kind, and a successful source-bound run receipt. Counts are producer tokens at commit 8d202439e, and the panel is generated by \breaktt {scripts/manuscript\_fig\_triple\_play.py}. Take-away: a model is authored once and then read, seen, and run from that single source.}}{11}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:triple_play}{{3}{11}{The Triple Play: one GNN text specification (left) and its three coordinated projections (right) --- the human-readable text form, graphical model visualizations, and executable simulation code. All three arrows originate at the same source box to show their shared parsed input. Source binding, parameter validation, and semantic-fidelity checks provide evidence of agreement among the projections. The executable node summarizes 12 of 12 registered render targets with implemented Step 12 execution adapters and previews three by name; execution depends on runtime readiness, admitted model kind, and a successful source-bound run receipt. Counts are producer tokens at commit 8d202439e, and the panel is generated by \protect \breaktt {scripts/manuscript\_fig\_triple\_play.py}. Take-away: a model is authored once and then read, seen, and run from that single source}{figure.caption.15}{}}
