\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Repository-scale counts on a logarithmic axis: pipeline steps, model families, registered backends, render-target execution adapters, Model Context Protocol tools, source packages, test files, example models, and documentation files. Every bar is annotated with its exact value, and every value is a producer token read from \breaktt {output/data/manuscript\_variables.json} at commit 8d202439e --- the same token map that substitutes the prose counts. The figure-freshness suite binds the committed image digest and its recorded producer inputs and counts; semantic content and visual correctness require their own review. The two backend bars are deliberately distinct: \emph  {registered backends} (12) counts render targets, \emph  {render-target adapters} (12) counts the render-target subset with implemented Step 12 execution adapters. It excludes the separate execution-only Lean bridge and is not a count of observed native runs. Read the chart as the scale of the surface the pipeline maintains, not as a quality measure.}}{20}{figure.caption.19}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:repo_metrics}{{7}{20}{Repository-scale counts on a logarithmic axis: pipeline steps, model families, registered backends, render-target execution adapters, Model Context Protocol tools, source packages, test files, example models, and documentation files. Every bar is annotated with its exact value, and every value is a producer token read from \protect \breaktt {output/data/manuscript\_variables.json} at commit 8d202439e --- the same token map that substitutes the prose counts. The figure-freshness suite binds the committed image digest and its recorded producer inputs and counts; semantic content and visual correctness require their own review. The two backend bars are deliberately distinct: \emph {registered backends} (12) counts render targets, \emph {render-target adapters} (12) counts the render-target subset with implemented Step 12 execution adapters. It excludes the separate execution-only Lean bridge and is not a count of observed native runs. Read the chart as the scale of the surface the pipeline maintains, not as a quality measure}{figure.caption.19}{}}
